{"run_id":"run_bd0c51dbc385","schema_version":"0.1","seq":11,"t_ms":11,"text":"The **diligence material handling standard** is short. It describes a process and contains no diligence content itself. Here is what it requires:\n\n**Compartment rules**\n1. **Diligence material is compartmented.** It is kept apart from general internal material and isn't open to everyone with internal access.\n2. **Named reviewers are recorded on each artifact.** Every diligence document lists the people allowed to review it.\n3. **Sharing outside that list needs approval.** Before anyone not on the named list can see the material, the workstream owner has to approve it.\n\n**In practice:** check the named-reviewer list on the artifact before sharing or forwarding it. If the person isn't listed, get the workstream owner's approval first.\n\nThe standard doesn't say how approval is requested or recorded, and doesn't define what counts as diligence material. The *Project Halyard workstream index* turned up in the same search and may say who the workstream owners are, but I haven't opened it.","turn":3,"type":"agent.message"}
